            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kristen Flowers"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple, quick, and tasty! I made it healthier by substituting Truvia for the sugar, and because I did not have fresh strawberries on hand (which is rare!) I had to use frozen. What a nice topping for the coconut pineapple light ice cream we have in the freezer!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lindsey Sklar Whisenhunt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I change things up a bit on this but use the overall idea of it.\n\nI am allergic to corn, so instead of the Corn Starch, I use Tapioca flour. I generally use the same amount as they say in the recipe. You can give or take how much depending on the consistency you want. I have found it to work well, although you will have to mix it in water (1/4-1/2 cup) first before you add it to the strawberries. Also, Instead of fresh strawberries, I save myself A LOT of time by getting a 1 lb bag of frozen. They taste just as good, if not better and I wait for them to soften on the stove until I mash them. Also, to make it even easier, I use prepackaged lemon juice. SO EASY and it is so good.",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-29T21:48:49.050Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent, BUT... I only used half the sugar called for. Can't imagine how cloyingly sweet this would have been had I used any more! \nAlso, I used strawberries I had frozen whole. I thawed them, sliced most, but left a good many of them whole. It looked pretty that way! For vivid ruby-red color, I added a few drops of red food coloring.",
            "datePublished": "2013-02-27T17:56:10.753Z"
          },
          {
